                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}.",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{2x+1}{3x+2}$, where $x\\ne0,-1,-\\dfrac12,-\\dfrac23$.",
          "worked": "Use part (b), then multiply numerator and denominator by $2x+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}&=\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{x+1}{2x+1}}\\\\\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}&=\\dfrac{2x+1}{(2x+1)+(x+1)}\\\\\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}&=\\dfrac{2x+1}{3x+2}.\\end{align*}$$\nRetain all original restrictions: $x\\ne0,-1,-\\dfrac12,-\\dfrac23$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q62-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Continue this pattern and simplify. What type of numbers are in the simplified expression?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Next: $\\dfrac{3x+2}{5x+3}$, where $x\\ne0,-1,-\\dfrac12,-\\dfrac23,-\\dfrac35$. The coefficients are Fibonacci numbers.\n\nEach new numerator is the previous denominator; the new denominator is the sum of the previous numerator and denominator.",
          "worked": "Using part (c), the next expression is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}}&=\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{2x+1}{3x+2}}\\\\\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}}&=\\dfrac{3x+2}{(3x+2)+(2x+1)}\\\\\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac{1}{1+\\dfrac1x}}}}&=\\dfrac{3x+2}{5x+3}.\\end{align*}$$\nAll nested denominators must remain nonzero, so $x\\ne0,-1,-\\dfrac12,-\\dfrac23,-\\dfrac35$.\n\nThe coefficients follow the Fibonacci numbers $1,1,2,3,5,\\ldots$: each is the sum of the preceding two. At each step, $\\frac{N}{D}$ becomes $\\frac{D}{D+N}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
